Repository Health Analyzer — retained dependency and provenance matrix

This file covers dependencies used by the standalone backend. Version pins are
recorded in uv.lock; upstream licenses remain with the installed distributions.

| Dependency | Purpose | Integration mode | License | Production required | Local copied source |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| FastAPI | REST transport | Python library | MIT | YES | NO |
| Pydantic | versioned contracts/validation | Python library | MIT | YES | NO |
| httpx | SourceCraft HTTP client | Python library | BSD-3-Clause | YES | NO |
| Uvicorn | ASGI runtime | Python library/entrypoint | BSD-3-Clause | YES | NO |
| structlog | structured logging | Python library | MIT/Apache-2.0 | YES | NO |
| PyDriller | Git history facts | Python library | BSD-3-Clause | YES | NO |
| Vale | documentation lint facts | external executable adapter | MIT | optional tool | NO |
| SonarQube | code-health facts | external service adapter | LGPL-3.0 / upstream terms | optional service | NO |
| git-sizer | repository-size facts | external executable adapter | MIT | optional tool | NO |

The repository's retained business source is covered by the root AGPL-3.0-or-
later license. The former `vendor/` copies are not runtime dependencies and are
removed as a whole; their notices are not silently reused as if they described
the retained Python package. Before a release that bundles an optional tool,
refresh its upstream notice and version-specific license record.
